  "prefLabel": "Env-Dw 901.04 Part-Specific Definitions",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-Dw 901.04 Part-Specific Definitions.\n\n(a) “Best management practice” means “best management practice” as defined in RSA 485-C:2, II, as reprinted in Appendix C.\n\n(b) “Boundary change” means the reclassification of some portion(s) of an area that has been reclassified pursuant to Env-Dw 901.06.\n\n(c) “Class” means class of groundwater.\n\n(d) “Contact person” means an individual who can be contacted on behalf of a local entity or other person who is submitting a request to the department regarding the request.\n\n(e) “Contributing area” means “contributing area” as defined in RSA 485-C:2, IV, as reprinted in Appendix C.\n\n(f) “Groundwater” means “groundwater” as defined in RSA 485-C:2, VIII, as reprinted in Appendix C.\n\n(g) “Inventory inspection” means a field verification conducted by the department or a local entity to determine whether an activity within the contributing area of a proposed groundwater reclassification that has been identified as a potential contamination source actually uses, handles, or stores regulated substances subject to the best management practices listed in Env-Wq 401.\n\n(h) “Local entity” means “local entity” as defined in RSA 485-C:2, X, as reprinted in Appendix C.\n\n(i) “Management inspection” means a periodic inspection conducted by a local entity to ensure that potential contamination source activities are in compliance with applicable best management practices.\n\n(j) “Person” means “person” as defined in RSA 485-C:2, XI, as reprinted in Appendix C.\n\n(k) “Potential contamination source” means “potential contamination sources” as described in RSA 485-C:7, as reprinted in Appendix C.\n\n(l) “Regulated contaminant” means “regulated contaminant” as defined in RSA 485-C:2, XIII, as reprinted in Appendix C.\n\n(m) “Regulated substance” means any of the following, with the exclusion of substances used for the treatment of drinking water or wastewater at department approved facilities:\n\n(1) Oil as defined in RSA 146-A:2, III, as reprinted in Appendix C;\n\n(2) Any substance that contains a regulated contaminant for which an ambient groundwater quality standard has been established pursuant to RSA 485-C:6; and\n\n(3) Any substance listed in 40 CFR 302, 7-1-24 edition.\n\n(n) “Wellhead protection area” means “wellhead protection area” as defined in RSA 485-C:2, XVIII, as reprinted in Appendix C.\n\nSource. (See Revision Note at part heading for Env-Dw 901) #8747, eff 10-28-06; ss by #10749, eff 12-19-14 (from Env-Dw 901.03); ss by #14296, eff 6-27-25, EXPIRES: 6-27-35",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-dw900.html"
